Description: local-first tree-structured note-taking application (egui version)
 OmaTree is a deliberately simple note-taking application: a tree of notes
 on the left and the selected note on the right. Every note can have child
 notes, so ideas branch the way your thinking does.
 .
 Notes are Markdown that you edit in place. A notebook is a single local
 file with the extension .omatree; there is no account and no cloud service.
 This is the egui version, which can be installed next to the Qt version
 ("omatree"). It saves notebooks as schema version 4, which older versions
 refuse to open.
